#
# Counter-example for gmeow:InventedWitnessShape: a chase-minted Skolem witness
# carrying TWO distinct gmeow:existentialOrdinal values, violating the
# documented invariant on gmeow:existentialOrdinal's own definition
# ("Single-valued per gmeow:InventedWitness") — a single Skolem witness
# discharges exactly one existential head-variable position of its firing
# rule, never two at once. gmeow:InventedWitnessShape's sh:maxCount 1 on
# gmeow:existentialOrdinal MUST reject it with
# shacl.MaxCountConstraintComponent (and no other finding — the datatype
# constraint is satisfied by both values, so maxCount is the sole violator).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecInventedWitnessTwoOrdinals).
# Lives under tests/ (NOT examples/) so the global make validate gate does not
# reject it.
#
# The trailing `gmeow:existentialOrdinal a owl:DatatypeProperty .` triple
# restates a fact already carried by diagnostics/module.ttl (harmless
# duplication) so THIS FILE's own term-reference set names the property, not
# only the class — the docs-coverage fixture-pair dimension credits a term by
# its CURIE appearing as a subject/object NamedNode in the fixture, and
# gmeow:existentialOrdinal is otherwise used only as a PREDICATE below.
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix owl:   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/diagnostics/tests/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

ex:witnessTwoOrdinals
    a gmeow:InventedWitness ;
    gmeow:existentialOrdinal "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ,
                             "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .

gmeow:existentialOrdinal a owl:DatatypeProperty .
